{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_ack", "label": "Ack (core primitive of reliable delivery)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fire-and-forget from controller to the producer's replyTo \u2014 the controller never awaits it, so the handler pays no latency for the Ack; a dropped Ack is recovered by retransmit plus dedup re-ack."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_ack_firing_sequence", "label": "How the ack actually fires", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_handler", "label": "Consumer handler(body)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only user-facing knob: everything inside handler(body) is your code, everything around it (dedup, ack, replyTo wiring, retransmit timing) is the controller's."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_persist_before_resolve", "label": "Persist before resolve", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Awaiting the journal write inside the handler makes the event and the implicit processed-seq marker durable together, so both crash windows resolve to zero duplication."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_throw_on_failure", "label": "Throw on failure (the only nack)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_producer_incarnation", "label": "Ack must echo the producer incarnation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "producerId and seq are guessable; the incarnation is not and leaves the producer only on deliveries it actually sent. Without the check anything able to address the producer could cancel the retransmit and fire confirm(null), downgrading the stream to at-most-once while reporting success."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_confirmation_callback", "label": "ConfirmationCallback / confirm(err)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only producer-side signal that a message landed; fires exactly once, never double-fires on a duplicate Ack, and for a redelivery means the handler ran on an earlier attempt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_reliabledelivery_facade", "label": "ReliableDelivery facade / ProducerHandle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_effectively_once", "label": "Effectively-once across consumer restart", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_sharded_consumer_dedup_reset", "label": "Sharded consumer loses dedup on rebalance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A moved entity gets a fresh ConsumerController with empty in-memory dedup, so without handler-side persistence every rebalance means full reprocessing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_slow_consumer_backpressure", "label": "Slow consumer / flow-control window", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_swallowing_errors_pitfall", "label": "Swallowing errors inside the handler", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A caught exception lets the handler resolve cleanly, so the controller Acks a message as done even though processing failed \u2014 let it propagate or persist the failure for a separate retry workflow."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_resend_timeout", "label": "resendTimeoutMs retransmit window", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_ack", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_ack_firing_sequence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/ack-semantics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_ack_semantics_ack_